{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists","id":1495915,"title":"Nova Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-30T15:16:20-07:00","id":1495915,"title":"Nova Antagonists","content":"I haven't seen any Named Nova stats anywhere. has something been put together or will i need to do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T15:29:30-07:00","id":1495916,"title":"","content":"The pre-errata version of the Proteus Novas Compendium was released on DriveThruRPG today. It has short bios for nearly 200 novas and stats for 28 Aberrant era characters.<br /> <br /> Some quick takeaways:<br /> <br /> Divis Mal is apparently nova Buddha. He has achieved enlightenment, but stuck around on this plane of existence for the sake of others.<br /> <br /> Count Orzaiz, charismatic spokesman for the Teragen, lacks any Mega Mental or Social Attributes, and in fact only has Intellect 1 and Presence 2. His skill as a talkshow talking head is apparently all mundane Skill, Skill Tricks, and Edges.<br /> <br /> None of the novas in the book seem to have any unique Tags attached to any of their powers, although a few have new Paths, which are detailed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 10-30-2022, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T16:54:19-07:00","id":1495921,"title":"","content":"so that would be a no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T19:15:45-07:00","id":1495932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1495916#post1495916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divis Mal is apparently nova Buddha. He has achieved enlightenment, but stuck around on this plane of existence for the sake of others.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Davis Mal </b>has stats beside bio in book? I will need his version from around N-Day time - but I can also reconstruct it from proper <b>Aberrant</b> times stats. ( Literally decade after N-Day. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-31-2022, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T19:30:45-07:00","id":1495933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1495932#post1495932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Davis Mal has stats beside bio in book? I will need his version from around N-Day time - but I can also reconstruct it from proper Aberrant times stats. ( Literally decade after N-Day. )</div> </div> </div> </div>His sidebar is about as big as his stat block, and explains that he has two modes of interaction, the stat block method in which he's holding himself back for the purpose of interacting with others in a manner they can understand, and the non-stat block method in which he stops bothering to roll dice pools because he's beyond that sort of thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, his stat block mostly amounts to Mega-Everything 1 + whatever Powers he feels like having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T12:43:30-07:00","id":1495997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1495916#post1495916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pre-errata version of the Proteus Novas Compendium was released on DriveThruRPG today. It has short bios for nearly 200 novas and stats for 28 Aberrant era characters.<br /> <br /> Some quick takeaways:<br /> <br /> Divis Mal is apparently nova Buddha. He has achieved enlightenment, but stuck around on this plane of existence for the sake of others.<br /> <br /> Count Orzaiz, charismatic spokesman for the Teragen, lacks any Mega Mental or Social Attributes, and in fact only has Intellect 1 and Presence 2. His skill as a talkshow talking head is apparently all mundane Skill, Skill Tricks, and Edges.<br /> <br /> None of the novas in the book seem to have any unique Tags attached to any of their powers, although a few have new Paths, which are detailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please be sure to submit any discrepancies, math errors, or the like to errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T16:47:46-07:00","id":1496012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1495997#post1495997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please be sure to submit any discrepancies, math errors, or the like to errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working on that right now. The process is an absolute nightmare. The first 43 pages weren't that bad, since they were just brief one or two paragraph background info write-ups, but I've spent the last four hours working on the stat block characters and am only four pages (and five characters) in, and one of those &quot;characters&quot; was a super abbreviated entry for a computer hacker organization. My best guess at this point is that every one of these entries was written by a different person, and that each writer formatted their entry in a different way without bothering to consult anyone else, with no actual proofreading before release.<br /> <br /> Three of the four characters have Armor entries. Each of them gets their armor from their Eufiber costume. The entries look like this:<br /> 1). Soft 1/Innocuous 2<br /> 2). Eufiber Clothing (Soft 1/ Innocuous)<br /> 3). Soft 1, Innocuous<br /> <br /> Three characters. Three formats for armor with the same source. All three are also wrong since Eufiber provides additional Armor Tags equal to the Eufiber dots, and they didn't add those.<br /> <br /> Three of the four have a Speed entry. That makes sense for two of them, since they have greater than normal speed, but Anteus and Rachel Alinsky both have Speed 1, and Anteus gets an entry while she doesn't. Additionally, either Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp's speed is a point to high or her Mega-Dexterity is a point to low.<br /> <br /> There are similar issues with other parts of the entries, but rather than summarize, I'll just copy/paste those issues directly from my master errata document:<br /> <br /> 45 Rachel Alinsky has Mega-Intellect 3, but doesn't have the three dots in free mental Edges that some with it, since her dots in Lightning Calculator come from her Technology Expert Path. Give her a total of 3 dots chosen from among Iron Will, Photographic Memory, and Speed Reading.<br /> <br /> 45 Rachel Alinsky has the Prolific Mega-Edge. This requires 2 dots in Mega-Cunning, while she only has 1 listed in either version of her stat block. It is also a leveled trait, but doesn't indicate how many levels she has in the first stat block, although it is listed as 2 dots in the Antagonist entry.<br /> <br /> 46 &quot;Their focus is on \u201cspreading thestories of fairness, justice, and truth \u2014 especially truth.\u201d<br /> Change &quot;thestories&quot; to &quot;stories&quot;<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp has the &quot;Ahead of Your Time&quot; Skill Trick despite not having enough dots in Technology or even being an inventor. This was probably an accidental cut/paste from Rachel Alinsky's entry. Replace &quot;Ahead of Your Time&quot; with an Athletics or Culture based Skill Trick.<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp's Followers Edge needs to include the two Tags associated with her Followers to maintain consistancy with the formatting of Elizabeth \u201cLondon Fog\u201d Barton's entry.<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp's &quot;Speed&quot; Mega-Edge should be &quot;Mega-Speed&quot;<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp has a &quot;Quantum Powers: None&quot; entry while Rachel Alinsky has no Quantum Powers entry at all. For the sake of consistancy, either both should have that entry or neither should have that entry.<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp's Transcendence entry has a dot instead of the number 1. It looks like almost every other entry in the book uses numbers for Transcendence instead of dots.<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp has a Speed entry of 5. If this is supposed to indicate speed scale, it should be 4 unless her Mega-Dexterity entry is wrong; with 1 base + 3 from the combination of her Mega-Dexterity and her Mega-Speed Mega-Edge.<br /> <br /> 47 Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp's Antagonist entry lacks her Fame, Followers, and Artistic Talent Edges, even though Antaeus' Antagonist entry kept his Fame Edge.<br /> <br /> 47 Dr. Spenser \u201cAntaeus\u201d Balmer has the Technique (Elemental Mastery (plants)) Mega-Edge, but the entry doesn't explain what Technique is granted. I assume the Technique is Elemental Mastery (plants): Quantum Anima, since making the corrections I'm about to submit to that entry make it a perfect rules fit as a Technique for Elemental Mastery (plants): Environmental Anima.<br /> <br /> 47 Dr. Spenser \u201cAntaeus\u201d Balmer's Environmental Anima entry has the &quot;(Variable 3)&quot; Tag. The power's entry on page 210 of Aberrant lists the Tag as Variable (1). This same error is repeated in his Antagonist entry on page 48.<br /> <br /> 47 Dr. Spenser \u201cAntaeus\u201d Balmer's Quantum Anima lists an entangle (2) Tag. This is unnecessary since the Grab Tag already creates an Entangle attack.<br /> <br /> 47 Dr. Spenser \u201cAntaeus\u201d Balmer has two Transformations, but no explanation for how they manifest, such as how Elizabeth \u201cLondon Fog\u201d Barton's entry describes her Transformations. Also, Transcendence 4 inflicts one Transformation. Is he meant to have more than the minimum number of required Transformations (which is entirely possible), or is this an error?<br /> <br /> 48 The Antagonist entry for Dr. Spenser \u201cAntaeus\u201d Balmer is missing a dot from his Photographic Memory Edge, as well as all of his Mega-Edges. I'm also not sure why you left out his Eufiber, Speed Reading, or Wealth Edges, especially since Adelheid \u201cDel\u201d Aveskamp's Antagonist Entry included her Wealth and Eufiber Edges.<br /> <br /> 48 The Antagonist entry for Dr. Spenser \u201cAntaeus\u201d Balmer is missing his Mega-Intellect and Quantum Anima powers.<br /> <br /> 48 Elizabeth \u201cLondon Fog\u201d Barton's Skill Tricks entry is formatted as &quot;Skill name (Skill Trick name),&quot; while all of the earlier entries just list Skill Trick names. While this entry certainly makes it easier to track down the Skill Tricks in the core book, consistancy should be maintained between entries. Either simplify this entry or expand the others to match formatting.<br /> <br /> 48 Elizabeth \u201cLondon Fog\u201d Barton's Followers Edge needs to delete the comma after the two dots but before the Follower Tags, and move those dots to after the Tags.<br /> <br /> 48 Elizabeth \u201cLondon Fog\u201d Barton's Mega-Edges and Powers entries are a convoluted mess.<br /> &quot;Technique (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Elemental Mastery)&quot; is both improperly formatted and has too many dots, since the Quantum Powers entry only has three listed powers total, meaning one is the base power and two are Techniques of that power. The entry should be written as Technique (Elemental Mastery) \u2022\u2022.<br /> Why does London Fog's entry include &quot;Power Suite 3&quot; when Anteus also has the Technique Mega-Edge but isn't listed as having &quot;Power Suite 2&quot;?<br /> The Quantum Powers entry for Environmental Anima does not tell the reader how many dots London Fog has in the power, and should replace &quot;Continuous, Continuous&quot; with &quot;Continuous (2)&quot;.<br /> The Quantum Powers entry for &quot;Quantum Attack (Destructive, Spread, Variable)&quot; does not tell the reader how many dots London Fog has in the power, and doesn't need the Variable Tag since 1) this is already part of a Power Suite and 2). the entry doesn't explain what Variable Tags are attached to the power. Deleting Variable also gives this Quantum Attack the same number of points in Tags as the next Technique.<br /> The Quantum Powers entry for &quot;Quantum Attack (Electrical, Brutal, Ranged \u2022) does not tell the reader how many dots London Fog has in the power, and Ranged \u2022 should be Ranged: Short).<br /> All of these changes should also be made to her Antagonist entry.<br /> <br /> 48 Elizabeth \u201cLondon Fog\u201d Barton's Transcendence entry has dots instead of the number 5. It looks like almost every other entry in the book uses numbers for Transcendence instead of dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 10-31-2022, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T04:30:39-07:00","id":1496032,"title":"","content":"Make sure you're putting all of that into the errata form. They don't pull errata from the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T08:15:46-07:00","id":1496040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496032#post1496032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sure you're putting all of that into the errata form. They don't pull errata from the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of efficiency, I compile a bunch of errata then spend an hour or so copy/pasting individual entries into the form and submitting them. I figure my current batch, which is now up to the Divis Mal entry, will get submitted either tonight or tomorrow.<br /> <br /> In further news, my continued proofreading efforts have now revealed that Pratima &quot;Splash&quot; Basham is both the third character in a row with the Technique Mega-Edge, and the third character in a row to format this edge/power suite in a fashion unrelated to the other write-ups, leading further credence to my theory that every single entry was written by a different person and that none of them bothered consulting each other. On the positive side, Splash's Technique write-up is much more understandable than the previous two, and I seriously hope the editors rework the other Technique entries to use her format.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T08:21:20-07:00","id":1496041,"title":"","content":"I dont see any such book in RPG","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T09:52:05-07:00","id":1496050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logansrun68</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496041#post1496041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont see any such book in RPG</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the pre-errata release for people who backed the Aberrant Kickstarter and got this book as a Stretch Goal. They're using us as unpaid proofreaders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Once our errata stops trickling in through their feedback form, they'll implement some of our corrections/feedback, fix the layout to adjust for the changes, and release a final version to everybody.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T10:32:25-07:00","id":1496055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496032#post1496032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sure you're putting all of that into the errata form. They don't pull errata from the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T10:37:48-07:00","id":1496056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496012#post1496012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My best guess at this point is that every one of these entries was written by a different person, and that each writer formatted their entry in a different way without bothering to consult anyone else, with no actual proofreading before release.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assure you this is not the case. Plenty of moving parts in a book this big and if there are mistakes in the sheets those typically fall directly to me. I greatly and deeply appreciate the feedback and effort, but please refrain from disparaging my team. Lots of folks worked very hard on this book, there are many moving parts, and there are bound to be errors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T14:18:26-07:00","id":1496064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496050#post1496050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the pre-errata release for people who backed the Aberrant Kickstarter and got this book as a Stretch Goal. They're using us as unpaid proofreaders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Once our errata stops trickling in through their feedback form, they'll implement some of our corrections/feedback, fix the layout to adjust for the changes, and release a final version to everybody.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> explains much thank you for explaning for me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T14:34:50-07:00","id":1496128,"title":"","content":"can anyone figure out how they are calculating the defense in these stat blocks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T18:08:51-07:00","id":1496145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496128#post1496128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can anyone figure out how they are calculating the defense in these stat blocks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Antagonist stat blocks are based on the category of the threat, modified by powers/armor as needed<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T20:36:51-07:00","id":1496149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496056#post1496056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can assure you this is not the case. Plenty of moving parts in a book this big and if there are mistakes in the sheets those typically fall directly to me. I greatly and deeply appreciate the feedback and effort, but please refrain from disparaging my team. Lots of folks worked very hard on this book, there are many moving parts, and there are bound to be errors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize if I came across as being disparaging of the writing team, as that was not my intent. I am fully aware that Onyx Path writers are freelancers and therefore are not initiating major content decisions regarding these books. If there are systematic issues regarding formatting in the stat blocks, it it likely a communications issue from higher up the command chain. I am mostly wondering why there are so many such issues with this particular book, when the N!WE and Novas Worldwide books both came out months ago and didn't have nearly this many stat block formatting issues during their public errata passes.<br /> <br /> It is difficult for me as a reader to provide proper errata form feedback when entries are so wildly variable that I frequently can't tell which of the formatting choices are purposeful and which are mistakes; and given that I spent ten years as a full time proofreader for a Tribune Company subsidiary in New York, followed by an additional ten years supplementing my income with occasional freelance reporting jobs for a Florida newspaper and a local business magazine, I can barely imagine the sort of problems faced by readers who lack such experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T20:48:08-07:00","id":1496151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496149#post1496149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if I came across as being disparaging of the writing team, as that was not my intent. I am fully aware that Onyx Path writers are freelancers and therefore are not initiating major content decisions regarding these books. If there are systematic issues regarding formatting in the stat blocks, it it likely a communications issue from higher up the command chain. I am mostly wondering why there are so many such issues with this particular book, when the N!WE and Novas Worldwide books both came out months ago and didn't have nearly this many stat block formatting issues during their public errata passes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I apologize if I came off overly defensive of them. At the end of the day, I am the dev on the book, and the buck stops here regarding formatting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496149#post1496149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is difficult for me as a reader to provide proper errata form feedback when entries are so wildly variable that I frequently can't tell which of the formatting choices are purposeful and which are mistakes; and given that I spent ten years as a full time proofreader for a Tribune Company subsidiary in New York, followed by an additional ten years supplementing my income with occasional freelance reporting jobs for a Florida newspaper and a local business magazine, I can barely imagine the sort of problems faced by readers who lack such experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how to respond to this exactly. Due to a whole host of issues (it's been a bit of a week) I still haven't gotten my hands on the copy that rolled out, so I'm not *exactly* sure what or where the errors are, but based on the discourse I'm seeing it's pretty clear I'll just have to do a ground up-reassessment of each individual entry, because clearly something went sideways somewhere. I appreciate the efforts on your part, and I can only apologize and assure you it will be corrected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-03T07:14:37-07:00","id":1496164,"title":"","content":"To be more precise in my question, for several of the entries, both the &quot;standard version&quot; and the &quot;antagonist version&quot; have defense higher than 1. Geryon, Tejido, and Tank are three examples. I understand the antagonist part, but not the &quot;standard version&quot; part. I was wondering if I had missed something in the rule set, or if this was an errata issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-03T07:18:37-07:00","id":1496165,"title":"","content":"I do really like the book! There are a few novas from 1e I was hoping to see that aren't included, but you can never get them all. There are also a lot of new faces/names/aliases. Overall, top-notch. Final post-errata product will be amazing! for those that don't have the preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-03T08:17:33-07:00","id":1496168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496164#post1496164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be more precise in my question, for several of the entries, both the &quot;standard version&quot; and the &quot;antagonist version&quot; have defense higher than 1. Geryon, Tejido, and Tank are three examples. I understand the antagonist part, but not the &quot;standard version&quot; part. I was wondering if I had missed something in the rule set, or if this was an errata issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely an errata issue on the player sheets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-03T08:18:06-07:00","id":1496169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496165#post1496165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do really like the book! There are a few novas from 1e I was hoping to see that aren't included, but you can never get them all. There are also a lot of new faces/names/aliases. Overall, top-notch. Final post-errata product will be amazing! for those that don't have the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T07:16:39-07:00","id":1496193,"title":"","content":"Will it be available for purchase soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27624-logansrun68","name":"logansrun68","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T09:52:51-07:00","id":1496204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logansrun68</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496193#post1496193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will it be available for purchase soon</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure maybe another few weeks for errata gathering. Some more weeks for review and input. A pass to make sure the changes didn't break layout. Get a PoD test printed. Review it. Approve it. Then it goes up for sale. So, I would guess we're a couple months out from seeing it released fully. Especially with the US holiday season kicking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T10:12:28-08:00","id":1496506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logansrun68</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1495915-nova-antagonists?p=1496193#post1496193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will it be available for purchase soon</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for books like these, they usually keep the errata document active for a week or two to get feedback. Once they either go through that period or they go about a week with no feedback, they close the form and move into errata implementation. Barring major problems, that'll usually take a few weeks before they put the final version up on DriveThruRPG.<br /> <br /> I just finished submitting the last of my errata to the form today. A quick count puts it at 237 submissions. Chapter one was pretty much just minor typographical problems that can be implemented in seconds without even messing up the layout. Chapter two had a large number of formatting issues, but most of that can be handled by changing numbers to dots or vice versa, moving stuff from one heading to another, or standardizing how certain things are presented (ie. None vs. N/A vs. no entry at all, Soft X/Hard X vs. Hard X/Soft X, etc.). The biggest problem there is if these changes alter the size of the entry enough to move things from one page to the next, thereby setting up a cascading layout problem.<br /> <br /> One layout issue they're going to have to find a way to work around is that two of the characters flat out don't work without reprinting the Selective (2) Tag from page 24 of Novas Worldwide.<br /> <br /> Violet &quot;Tank&quot; Chao has the power to protect crowds of bystanders via Quantum Deflection. The problem there is that neither of the current tags (Impervious and Range) appear to be appropriate. The Impervious Tag is meant to allow armor to counter Piercing attacks, but Quantum Deflection doesn't provide armor, it raises Defense. Range is meant to increase the range of an attack that affects others, but Quantum Deflection is a personal power. In order to get it to do what they want, they have to swap the tags for Area (4) to target everyone within Short range (approx. 100 feet) of Chao, then add Selective (2) from Novas Worldwide so she's only protecting bystanders instead of bad guys.<br /> <br /> Jennifer &quot;Slider&quot; Landers has Teleport with the Distance, Area, and Impose Tags. Distance lets her teleport anywhere on Earth, Area lets her affect multiple people, and Impose lets her teleport others with a touch. Good so far, but Area affects everyone in range. Every time she teleports herself, everyone in range rolls to resist or they come along for the ride. Every time she teleports someone else via touch, everyone in range rolls to resist or they come along for the ride (including her). She needs that Selective Tag so she can choose who does and does not get teleported.<br /> <br /> So somewhere in this book, they'll have to add a sidebar with that Tag. Maybe they can stick it in the empty space after Cestus Pax's entry and add a (p. xx) pointer in the character entries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T12:54:50-08:00","id":1501046,"title":"","content":"Why not rework fictional characters for antagonists?<br /> <br /> Dolores Umbridge wouldn't be that hard to make into a truly brutal Nova. Power mad and ice hearted, a monster in anyone's book.<br /> <br /> Squire Trelaine (Squire of Gothos) a powerful Nova with a lack of responsibility and maturity would be scary.<br /> <br /> Becky Sharp isn't evil but she is ruthless, callous, and narrowly focused. Her goal wouldn't be the issue, it's the collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Ralph Nickelby was self centered and cold. The one time someone penetrated his shell led to his suicide. Ralph would follow his goal to destruction. <br /> <br /> Uncle Charlie from <b>Shadow of a Doubt. </b>He was a serial killer with a twisted moral vision. His charm masked his venom. <br /> <br /> Merlin from <b>Last Defender of Camelot. </b>A fanatic with power and charm. His pursuit of justice is noble, his inability to acknowledge collateral damage makes him a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T12:58:46-08:00","id":1501047,"title":"","content":"El Dorado from the old <b>Super Friends </b>TV show is really a scary opponent. Invisibility, telepathy, teleportation, and illusion projection. It wouldn't be long until he got the PCs to kill each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}